/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
.DS_Store
/node_modules
/dist

# `tools/oracle` is deliberately outside the workspace (see its README), so its
# build artefacts are not covered by the `/target` line above. Its lock file is
# not committed because it resolves against a sibling checkout of
# `data-modelling-sdk` and would churn with that repository rather than with
# this one; what pins the oracle for reproducibility is the SDK commit recorded
# inside each generated verdicts file.
/tools/oracle/target
/tools/oracle/Cargo.lock

# `tools/headergen` and `tools/sanitise` are outside the workspace for the same
# reason `tools/oracle` is, so their build output needs its own lines too.
#
# `tools/headergen/Cargo.lock`, unlike the oracle's, IS committed: it pins
# `cbindgen`, and an unpinned generator would let a `cbindgen` release fail the
# header-drift test without anybody having changed an ABI.
/tools/headergen/target
/tools/sanitise/build

# The generated site. `website/build.sh` rebuilds it from `specs.toml` and the
# member manifests, so committing it would be committing a second copy of the
# registry — exactly what this crate exists to avoid.
/website/dist
